<title>USA: Iraq still negotiating U.S. wheat tender - US trade.</title>
<headline>Iraq still negotiating U.S. wheat tender - US trade.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1997-04-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Iraq was still negotiating the purchase of 50,000 tonnes of U.S. hard red winter wheat under a United Nations-monitored oil-for-food deal, U.S. exporters said on Friday.</p>
<p>The tender, set for Friday, was not done yet, one exporter said. &quot;I think they are waiting for the flat price to fall back.&quot;</p>
<p>Another exporter said Iraq was looking at offers right now. &quot;The tender was valid until Tuesday,&quot; he said.</p>
<p>A third exporter agreed.</p>
<p>&quot;They have not bought anything. I'm sure it will be over the weekend,&quot; he said.</p>
<p>The wheat would be for June arrival.</p>
<p>((Doris Frankel 312-983-7305))</p>
